        "original_id": "ca803839-d771-5dd9-a6c9-2f436e097ff7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport, Cheyenne Regional Airport, Little Rock, Cheyenne, Laramie County, Wyoming\n- Products: Pinnacle Airlines Flight 3701, Cessna 177B Cardinal\n- People: Jessica Dubroff\n- Concepts: civil-military airports, international airports, flight crashes\n\nFacts:\n- Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport is also known as Wold–Chamberlain Field and is a joint civil-military public-use international airport.\n- Cheyenne Regional Airport, also called Jerry Olson Field, is a civil-military airport one mile north of downtown Cheyenne in Laramie County, Wyoming.\n- Pinnacle Airlines Flight 3701 was an overnight repositioning flight with no passengers from Little Rock, Arkansas, to Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport, and both crew members were killed.\n- On the second day of Jessica Dubroff’s quest, a Cessna 177B Cardinal piloted by her flight instructor crashed in a rainstorm immediately after takeoff from Cheyenne Regional Airport in Cheyenne, Wyoming, killing Jessica Dubroff, her 57-year-old father, and her flight instructor.",
